  "problem": "The durations of direct flights on a certain route are normally distributed with a mean of $180$ minutes and a standard deviation of $20$ minutes. What is the probability that a randomly selected flight lasts more than $178$ minutes but less than $188$ minutes? **Round your answer to two decimal places**.\n\n*Hint: A table of values of $\u03a6(z)$ for different values of $z$ is given below, where $\u03a6(z)$ is the cumulative distribution function for the standard normal distribution. *\n\n| | $z$ | $\\,0.00\\,$ | $\\,0.01\\,$ | $\\,0.02\\,$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $\\,-0.2\\,$ | $\\,0.4207\\,$ | $\\,0.4168\\,$ | $\\,0.4129\\,$ |\n| $\\,-0.1\\,$ | $\\,0.4602\\,$ | $\\,0.4562\\,$ | $\\,0.4522\\,$ |\n| $\\,0.0\\,$ | $\\,0.5000\\,$ | $\\,0.4960\\,$ | $\\,0.4920\\,$ | |  | | $z$ | $\\,0.00\\,$ | $\\,0.01\\,$ | $\\,0.02\\,$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $\\,0.2\\,$ | $\\,0.5793\\,$ | $\\,0.5832\\,$ | $\\,0.5871\\,$ |\n| $\\,0.3\\,$ | $\\,0.6179\\,$ | $\\,0.6217\\,$ | $\\,0.6255\\,$ |\n| $\\,0.4\\,$ | $\\,0.6554\\,$ | $\\,0.6591\\,$ | $\\,0.6628\\,$ | |  |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $z$ | $\\,0.00\\,$ | $\\,0.01\\,$ | $\\,0.02\\,$ |\n| $\\,-0.2\\,$ | $\\,0.4207\\,$ | $\\,0.4168\\,$ | $\\,0.4129\\,$ |\n| $\\,-0.1\\,$ | $\\,0.4602\\,$ | $\\,0.4562\\,$ | $\\,0.4522\\,$ |\n| $\\,0.0\\,$ | $\\,0.5000\\,$ | $\\,0.4960\\,$ | $\\,0.4920\\,$ |\n| $z$ | $\\,0.00\\,$ | $\\,0.01\\,$ | $\\,0.02\\,$ |\n| $\\,0.2\\,$ | $\\,0.5793\\,$ | $\\,0.5832\\,$ | $\\,0.5871\\,$ |\n| $\\,0.3\\,$ | $\\,0.6179\\,$ | $\\,0.6217\\,$ | $\\,0.6255\\,$ |\n| $\\,0.4\\,$ | $\\,0.6554\\,$ | $\\,0.6591\\,$ | $\\,0.6628\\,$ |\n\nThe probability that a randomly selected flight lasts more than $178$ minutes but less than $188$ minutes is approximately\n{{field-1}}.",
